TEXT 0 -220 Left 2 ;Lab A part 3 - Soft link, WITH the air load: baffled-piston radiation impedance on BOTH faces of each cone
TEXT 0 -188 Left 2 ;coupling per cone: G_a injects U = S*u into the acoustic node, G_m draws the reaction force f = S*p from the velocity node
TEXT 0 230 Left 2 ;acoustic side, IMPEDANCE analogy: node voltage = pressure [Pa] (sum of both faces), current = volume velocity [m3/s]
TEXT 0 700 Left 2 ;reference: the same speaker WITHOUT air (part 1), for the overlay
TEXT 0 1040 Left 2 !.param Mmvc=6m Cmsp=1.3m Rmsp=0.5 Mmd=5m Cmsr=2.7m Rmsr=0.22\n.param Cmd_st=1e-10 Rmd_st=5000 Cmd_so=3e-6 Rmd_so=5\n.param Si=60e-4 So=210e-4\n.param MA1i=7.2954 RA1i=29835.1 RA2i=67653.3 CA1i=3.5505e-09\n.param MA1o=3.8996 RA1o=8524.32 RA2o=19329.5 CA1o=2.3248e-08
TEXT 0 1180 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 10 10k
TEXT 0 1230 Left 2 ;3a: V(u_vc) V(u_d) vs V(u_vc_ref) V(u_d_ref);  Z_M = 1/V(u_vc).   3b: front pressure = V(p_i)/2 and V(p_o)/2;
TEXT 0 1262 Left 2 ;far field 1 m, half space: 2*pi*frequency*1.18*(60e-4*V(u_vc)+210e-4*V(u_d))/(2*pi*1)
